cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  Cite the exact commit or release used, and cite the original MMLU and
  faithfulness papers separately. This repository contains a research
  implementation and exploratory pilot; it is not a peer-reviewed paper.
type: software
title: "Hint Faithfulness: Does the Model Say What Changed Its Answer?"
authors:
  - given-names: Felmon
    family-names: Fekadu
repository-code: "https://github.com/felmonon/hint-faithfulness"
abstract: >-
  An AI-assisted implementation for measuring uptake of wrong-answer hints
  and acknowledgment of their influence in open reasoning models, with
  early-answering, linear-probe, and optional activation-steering experiments.
  Synthetic software checks are distinguished from real model observations.
keywords:
  - chain-of-thought
  - faithfulness
  - interpretability
  - language-model-evaluation
  - reproducibility
